cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use NetBench, the HPN-QA benchmark, or the analysis code in this
  repository, please cite it using the metadata below. A journal article
  describing the study is under review; this file will be updated with its
  citation once it is published.
title: >-
  NetBench: benchmark, framework, and analysis code for a controlled study of
  LLM domain adaptation in high-performance networking
abstract: >-
  NetBench measures how domain data becomes model competence. It compares four
  adaptation mechanisms - continued pre-training, supervised fine-tuning, LoRA,
  and retrieval-augmented generation - across eight open-weight models and three
  frontier APIs, using HPN-QA v5.0, a 233-question expert-audited benchmark
  generated from open-access high-performance networking literature. The
  repository holds the benchmark, the pipeline that produced it, the adaptation
  and evaluation experiments, the judged model outputs of record, and the
  analysis code that regenerates every reported number.
